bol (MANDATORY PROPS)\n    19\t\n    20\tUse the `<chip />` primitive.\n    21\t\n    22\t  * **Footprint:** Pass the imported variable to the `footprint` prop.\n    23\t  * **Pin Mapping:** Use `pinLabels` to map physical pin numbers to datasheet names.\n    24\t  * **Mandatory Prop Handling:**\n    25\t      * **Rule:** Your component **MUST** extend `CommonLayoutProps` and spread `{...props}` onto the underlying `<chip />`.\n    26\t      * **Reason:** This allows the parent circuit to control positioning (`schX`, `pcbX`) and rotation.\n    27\t\n    28\t### C. Standard Component Template\n    29\t\n    30\t**File:** `lib/Components/GenericControllerIC.tsx`\n    31\t\n    32\t```typescript\n    33\timport type { CommonLayoutProps } from "tscircuit"\n    34\timport QFP_Footprint from "../footprints/QFP32_Generic.kicad_mod"\n    35\t\n    36\t// 1. MANDATORY: Interface must extend CommonLayoutProps\n    37\tinterface Props extends CommonLayoutProps {\n    38\t  name: string\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\texport const GenericControllerIC = (props: Props) => {\n    42\t  return (\n    43\t    <chip\n    44\t      footprint={QFP_Footprint}\n    45\t      pinLabels={{\n    46\t        pin1: "VDD",\n    47\t        pin2: "GND",\n    48\t        // ... mappings\n    49\t        pin32: "VSS"\n    50\t      }}\n    51\t      // 2. CRITICAL: Spread props to enable positioning\n    52\t      {...props}\n    53\t    />\n    54\t   )\n    55\t}\n    56\t```\n    57\t\n    58\t-----\n    59\t\n    60\t## 2. Modular Circuit Design with `<group />`\n    61\t\n    62\tThe `<group />` element is a container used to organize multiple components into a single block. It is highly recommended to use `<group>` with **Flex** or **Grid** props to handle layout automatically, rather than calculating manual coordinates for every sub-component.\n    63\t\n    64\t### A. Creating a Reusable Module\n    65\t\n    66\tWrap related components and traces inside a `<group />`.\n    67\t\n    68\t  * **Mandatory Prop Handling:** Your Module **MUST** accept `CommonLayoutProps` and spread them onto the root `<group>` tag.\n    69\t\n    70\t**File:** `lib/Modules/PowerInput.tsx`\n    71\t\n    72\t```typescript\n    73\timport type { CommonLayoutProps } from "tscircuit"\n    74\t\n    75\tinterface Props extends CommonLayoutProps {\n    76\t  namePrefix?: string \n    77\t}\n    78\t\n    79\texport const PowerInputModule = (props: Props) => {\n    80\t  return (\n    81\t    // CRITICAL: Spread props here to allow moving the whole group\n    82\t    <group {...props}>\n    83\t      {/* Passives must have a footprint and name */}\n    84\t      <resistor name="R_Fuse" resistance="10" footprint="0603" schX={0} schY={0} />\n    85\t      <capacitor name="C_Bulk" capacitance="100uF" footprint="1206" schX={10} schY={0} />\n    86\t      \n    87\t      {/* Internal connections */}\n    88\t      <trace from=".R_Fuse > .pin2" to=".C_Bulk > .pos" />\n    89\t    </group>\n    90\t  )\n    91\t}\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\t### B. Auto-Layout (Grid & Flex)\n    95\t\n    96\tUse these props on the `<group>` tag to arrange children automatically without manual X/Y math.\n    97\t\n    98\t  * **Schematic Layout:** `schFlex`, `schFlexDirection` (row/column), `schGap`.\n    99\t  * **PCB Layout:** `pcbGrid`, `pcbGridCols`, `pcbGridGap`.\n   100\t\n   101\t**Example (Auto-arranged LEDs):**\n   102\t\n   103\t```typescript\n   104\t<group \n   105\t  schFlex schFlexDirection="column" schGap="2mm" \n   106\t  pcbGrid pcbGridCols={2} pcbGridGap="1mm"\n   107\t  {...props}\n   108\t>\n   109\t    <led name="LED1" color="red" footprint="0603" />\n   110\t    <led name="LED2" color="green" footprint="0603" />\n   111\t    <led name="LED3" color="blue" footprint="0603" />\n   112\t    <led name="LED4" color="yellow" footprint="0603" />\n   113\t</group>\n   114\t```\n   115\t\n   116\t-----\n   117\t\n   118\t## 3. Circuit Assembly and Connectivity\n   119\t\n   120\t### A. Instantiation & Placement\n   121\t\n   122\t  * **Container:** `<board width="..." height="...">`.\n   123\t  * **Primitives:** Use built-in lowercase elements (e.g., `<resistor />`, `<capacitor />`) directly. **Do not import them.**\n   124\t  * **Positioning:** Use `schX`/`schY` (schematic) and `pcbX`/`pcbY` (PCB) on components or groups.\n   125\t\n   126\t### B. Connectivity\n   127\t\n   128\t  * **Direct Trace:** `<trace from=".U1 > .pin1" to=".R1 > .pin2" />`\n   129\t  * **Power Nets:** Use `<net name="VCC" />`. Connect pins to `net.VCC`.\n   130\t\n   131\t### C. Assembly Template\n   132\t\n   133\t**File:** `index.tsx`\n   134\t\n   135\t```typescript\n   136\timport { GenericControllerIC } from "./lib/Components/GenericControllerIC"\n   137\timport { PowerInputModule } from "./lib/Modules/PowerInput"\n   138\t\n   139\texport default () => {\n   140\t  return (\n   141\t    <board width="100mm" height="80mm">\n   142\t      <net name="VCC" />\n   143\t      <net name="GND" />\n   144\t\n   145\t      {/* 1. Place the Power Module */}\n   146\t      <PowerInputModule schX={-20} schY={0} pcbX={-20} pcbY={10} />\n   147\t\n   148\t      {/* 2. Place the Main IC */}\n   149\t      <GenericControllerIC name="U_Main" schX={20} schY={0} pcbX={20} pcbY={10} />\n   150\t\n   151\t      {/* 3. Place a decoupling capacitor (Standard Element) */}\n   152\t      <capacitor \n   153\t         name="C_Decouple" \n   154\t         capacitance="100nF" \n   155\t         footprint="0402" \n   156\t         schX={20} schY={10} \n   157\t      />\n   158\t\n   159\t      {/* 4. Global Connections */}\n   160\t      <trace from=".U_Main > .VDD" to="net.VCC" />\n   161\t      <trace from=".U_Main > .GND" to="net.GND" />\n   162\t      <trace from=".C_Decouple > .pin1" to="net.VCC" />\n   163\t      <trace from=".C_Decouple > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n   164\t    </board>\n   165\t  )\n   166\t}\n   167\t```\n   168\t\n   169\t-----\n   170\t\n   171\t## 4. Built-in Elements in `tscircuit`\n   172\t\n   173\tThese elements are available globally. You do not need to import them.\n   174\t\n   175\t| Element | Description/Usage |\n   176\t| :--- | :--- |\n   177\t| `<board />` | Root container for all components and traces. |\n   178\t| `<chip />` | Generic component for ICs with custom footprints/pin mappings. |\n   179\t| `<resistor />` | Limits current. **Requires `footprint` (e.g., "0402"), `resistance`, `name`.** |\n   180\t| `<capacitor />` | Stores energy/filters. **Requires `footprint`, `capacitance`, `name`.** |\n   181\t| `<inductor />` | Stores energy in magnetic field. **Requires `footprint`, `inductance`, `name`.** |\n   182\t| `<diode />` | Rectification/protection. **Requires `footprint`, `name`.** |\n   183\t| `<led />` | Light emitting diode. **Requires `footprint`, `color`, `name`.** |\n   184\t| `<transistor />` | Generic three-terminal amplification/switching device. |\n   185\t| `<mosfet />` | Field-effect transistor (Switching). |\n   186\t| `<crystal />` | Clock signal source. |\n   187\t| `<switch />` / `<pushbutton />` | Mechanical connection controls. |\n   188\t| `<jumper />` / `<solderjumper />` | Configuration bridges. |\n   189\t| `<trace />` | Connects two points (`from`, `to`). |\n   190\t| `<net />` | Groups traces into a named node (e.g., "VCC", "GND"). |\n   191\t| `<via />` | Plated hole connecting PCB layers. |\n   192\t| `<footprint />` | Defines physical layout (used internally or for custom parts). |\n   193\t| `<pinheader />` | Connector for external interfaces. |\n   194\t| `<group />` | Container for organizing elements. Supports Flex/Grid layouts. |\n   195\t| `<subcircuit />` | Tightly coupled functional block with isolated nets/autorouting. |\n   196\t| `<testpoint />` | Layout feature for electrical testing. |\n   197\t| `<hole />` | Non-conductive mounting hole. |\n   198\t\n   199\t-----\n   200\t\n   201\t## 5. Agent Instructions for "Text-to-Circuit"\n   202\t\n   203\tWhen generating code:\n   204\t\n   205\t1.  **Define Nets:** If standard rails (VCC, GND) are needed, instantiate `<net />` elements first.\n   206\t2.  **Passives:** Use standard tags (e.g., `<resistor />`) but **ALWAYS** specify a `footprint` (e.g., "0402", "0603") and a `name`.\n   207\t3.  **Modules:** Use `<group>` with `schFlex`/`pcbGrid` props to arrange components automatically.\n   208\t4.  **Mandatory Props:** Ensure ALL custom components and groups accept `CommonLayoutProps` and spread `{...props}` to the root element.\n   209\t5.  **Connect:** Use point-to-point traces for signals and nets for power.\n'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_e60cd75d85264e5196c6f83281a8', 'name': 'file_editor'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_fda981f19ef24ed3a27b80eb6948', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'think', 'arguments': '{"thought": "I will start by creating the `index.tsx` file in the `ana/output` directory. I\'ll follow the BFS-DC method, starting with the main IC (U1: BQ79616PAPR) and then expanding to its connected components.\\n\\nAnchor 1: U1 (BQ79616PAPR)\\nAnchor 2: U2 (ISO7342FCQDWRQ1)\\n\\nI\'ll organize the circuit into groups for better structure:\\n1. Main IC & Decoupling\\n2. NPN Supply (Q1)\\n3. Temperature Sensing (GPIOs)\\n4. Communication (Isolated & Direct)\\n5. Auxiliary Measurement (BBP/BBN)\\n6. Cell Configuration (Jumpers)\\n\\nI\'ll use the local library components as identified in the SCUD.\\n\\nWait, I need to check the pinout of the components in the library to ensure correct connectivity. I\'ll view the library files."}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Your thought has been logged.'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_fda981f19ef24ed3a27b80eb6948', 'name': 'think'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_95a1507f3ede470584afd2e0e57f', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'file_editor', 'arguments': '{"security_risk": "LOW", "path": "/home/pst/Documents/VHL_ANA/virtual_hardware_laboratary/imports/B